@crew lindqvist-isak
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hey. Lindqvist, helm. She's pulling left today. Don't worry, I've got her.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hey, {me}. Rowing later? I'm chasing the Commander's time.
- Oh, hey, {me}. My turn with the guitar book. It's always my turn.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. Sit still for once. You and me both.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Felt a drift before the console did. Corrected it. Nobody even noticed. Perfect.
? mood:low
- Restless day. I rowed. Then I rowed again.
== near
? act:gym
- The Commander's moved to the treadmill. Scared of me, I reckon.   #funny
? habit:music
- Music room. Don't listen too closely. The guitar and I are still arguing.   #funny
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I can feel a drift in our course before the console shows it. Like a tilt in your tea.
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- A smooth turn. The whole ship leans, just a hair, and nobody spills a drop.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 3: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, bye, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue, hint, about, life)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning, {me}! Rowed before breakfast. Still not top. Yet.
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- {me}! Where've you been? Never mind. Rowing later? You owe me a race.

== bye
- {bye}. Walk fast. Life's short and the corridor's long.   #funny

== near
? habit:window-seat
- Window seat. I can feel us drift. The window just proves it.
? deck:1
- She's steady today. Barely a hair off. I've got her.

== invite
- Rowing after shift? Five hundred metres. Loser buys the tea.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Friday jam? I'll play. Badly. Park's worse. Come and decide.   #funny

== accept
- Yes! Good. Don't be late. I'll be early. And restless.   #funny
- Course. I'm in.

== decline
- Can't. Rowing. Moreau's two seconds ahead. Not having it.
? weekday:mon|tue
- Rest day. I'm going to try sitting still. Tuesday? If I survive.   #funny

== missed
- You didn't come. I rowed anyway. Faster, actually. Thanks?   #funny

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday! You can have the guitar book for a whole day. Huge.   #funny
? birthday:me
- My birthday. Park let me keep the guitar book all day. Best present. Still bad, though.   #funny

== cue
? cue:event.ionStorm.onset
- Storm's in. She'll buck a bit. I've got her. Hold on to something.

== hint
- Hey, {me}. Got a minute later? I've something to say. I'll even sit still.

== about
? aff:park-noor:friend
- Park and I share the guitar book. We're both bad. Best hour of my week.   #warm

== life
? tier>=friend
- I've never sat still. On the helm I don't have to. She moves, I move. Perfect.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 6: bubbles (smalltalk, rumour), at most one in five about work. 60 characters.
== smalltalk
- Rowing later. Chasing a time.
- My turn with the guitar book.   #funny
- Can't sit still. Never could.
? act:meal
- Eat fast, row faster.   #funny
? deck:1
- She's pulling left. Got her.
?

== rumour
- Quick, before I forget.
- You'll want this. Quick version.

// Writer 4, batch 12: goodbyes (leaving:you), packing (leaving:soon) and letters after they've moved on.
== feel
? leaving:soon
- Packing. Fast. The guitar's coming. The book isn't. It's the Wren's.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- Off soon. Bet you can't beat my rowing time while I'm gone.
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- You never let me win. Good. That's why it counted. Cheers.   #warm

== letter
- New ship. The helm pulls right, not left. Strange. The guitar's still bad. The rowing board's mine.
? tier>=friend
- Played a whole song today. Start to finish. Badly. Thought of the music room's book.
